  "notes": "Merchants house (3×3, D-054/D-056; design review: richer than the citizens house at a glance): two full storeys plus an attic — a stone ground floor with quoins, a string course, a shop window and a door, a jettied half-timbered first floor (posts, rails and St Andrew's crosses), a steep roof with attic windows in the gable or two dormers, a chimney and a shop sign with an emblem on an iron bracket. v0 red tiles, dark timber, an oriel; v1 shingles, ox-blood timber on ochre plaster, a flowered balcony and an awning stall; v2 ochre tiles, light timber, an oriel and a small balcony.",
